        "lessons": [
          {
            "title": "Lesson #1",
            "id": 148378,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why do we pass a function as a parameter inside of <code>.map()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">To tell the <code>.map()</code> function how to transform each game value</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">To tell the <code>.map()</code> function which array to transform</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">To tell the <code>.map()</code> function how many items are in the calling array</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">To tell the <code>.map()</code> function how to transform each game value.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #2",
            "id": 148379,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code a return statement that converts each player health value (out of 100) to a percentage.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"index\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"92\" endIndex=\"98\" /><option startIndex=\"99\" endIndex=\"106\" /><option startIndex=\"107\" endIndex=\"108\" /><option startIndex=\"109\" endIndex=\"112\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" health = [\" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"60\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"75\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" healthPercent = health.map(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" element / \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(healthPercent);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>return</code> followed by <code>element</code> and then <code>/</code>, <code>100</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #3",
            "id": 148380,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code an arrow function that adds 10% bonus score to each value in the <code>scores</code> array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"55\" endIndex=\"61\" /><option startIndex=\"62\" endIndex=\"65\" /><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option startIndex=\"72\" endIndex=\"73\" /><option startIndex=\"73\" endIndex=\"74\" /><option startIndex=\"75\" endIndex=\"86\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" scores = [\" /><text value=\"1200\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"850\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"400\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"2150\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" boosted = scores.map(\" /><text value=\"score\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\" =&gt;\" /><text value=\" score * \" /><text value=\"1.1\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\");\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(boosted);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>scores</code> followed by <code>map</code> and then <code>score</code>, <code>=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>score * 1.1</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #4",
            "id": 148381,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What is the correct syntax for calling <code>.map()</code> on an array named <code>enemies</code>.</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The array name followed by <code>.map()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The <code>.map()</code> function followed by the array name</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The <code>.map()</code> function with the array name passed as a parameter</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The array name followed by <code>.map()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #5",
            "id": 148382,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the syntax for calling the <code>.map()</code> function on the <code>hitPoints</code> array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"51\" endIndex=\"64\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" hitPoints = [\" /><text value=\"10\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"31\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"42\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"73\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" isEven = hitPoints.map(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\" =&gt;\" /><text value=\" (element % \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\" == \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"));\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(isEven);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>hitPoints.map</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #6",
            "id": 148383,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why do we pass a function as a parameter inside of <code>.filter()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">To tell the <code>.filter()</code> function which game objects to keep or remove in the new array</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">To tell the <code>.filter()</code> function which array to modify</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">To tell the <code>.filter()</code> function how to transform each element</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">To tell the <code>.filter()</code> function which game objects to keep or remove in the new array.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #7",
            "id": 148384,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What is the correct syntax for calling <code>.filter()</code> on an array named <code>items</code>.</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The array name followed by <code>.filter()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The <code>.filter()</code> function followed by the array name</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The <code>.filter()</code> function with the array name passed as a parameter</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The array name followed by <code>.filter()</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #8",
            "id": 148385,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the syntax for calling the <code>.filter()</code> function on the <code>loot</code> array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"61\" endIndex=\"72\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" loot = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Torch&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Token&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Potion&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Trap&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" T = loot.filter(\" /><text value=\"element\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\" =&gt;\" /><text value=\" (element[\" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"] === \" /><text value=\"&quot;T&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"));\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(T);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>loot.filter</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #9",
            "id": 148386,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Add the inline function declaration and appropriate parameter to populate the <code>bossDamage</code> array using <code>.filter()</code>.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"100\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" enemyDamage = [\" /><text value=\"99\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"56\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"78\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"110\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"29\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"58\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" bossDamage = enemyDamage.filter(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"total\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total &gt; \" /><text value=\"80\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>function(total)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #10",
            "id": 148387,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Examine the parameters and complete the syntax such that <code>first3</code> stores the first three <code>spawnQueue</code> enemies.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"127\" endIndex=\"132\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" spawnQueue = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;Slime&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Bat&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Goblin&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Orc&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;Mage&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" first3 = spawnQueue.filter(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"name, index\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" index &lt; \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(first3);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>index</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #11",
            "id": 148388,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why do we pass a function as a parameter inside of <code>.reduce()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">To tell the <code>.reduce()</code> function how to combine the game values into one result</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">To tell the <code>.reduce()</code> function which array to modify</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">To tell the <code>.reduce()</code> function which elements to keep or remove</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">To tell the <code>.reduce()</code> function how to combine the game values into one result.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #12",
            "id": 148389,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Complete the syntax for calling the <code>.reduce()</code> function on the <code>coinPickups</code> array.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" startIndex=\"60\" endIndex=\"78\" isDefault=\"true\" /></interactions><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" coinPickups = [\" /><text value=\"20\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"21\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"12\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"13\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" totalCoins = coinPickups.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prevVal + currVal;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(totalCoins);}\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>coinPickups.reduce</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #13",
            "id": 148390,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What is the minimum amount of parameters we need to make <code>.reduce()</code> work?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">2</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">3</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">1</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick 2.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #14",
            "id": 148391,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Code an arrow function that takes two parameters ( <code>prev</code> and <code>curr</code> ) and returns their sum.</p><code name=\"script.js\" version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\"><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"comboHits\" /></content></option><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"68\" /><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"72\" endIndex=\"73\" /><option startIndex=\"74\" endIndex=\"78\" /><option startIndex=\"78\" endIndex=\"79\" /><option startIndex=\"80\" endIndex=\"82\" /><option startIndex=\"83\" endIndex=\"94\" /></options></interaction></interactions><content><text value=\"var\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" comboHits = [\" /><text value=\"250\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"125\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"465\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"var\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" comboTotal = comboHits.reduce(\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prev, curr\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" prev + curr);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(comboTotal);\" /></content></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>(</code> followed by <code>prev</code> and then <code>,</code>, <code>curr</code>, <code>)</code>, <code>=&gt;</code>, <code>prev + curr</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Lesson #15",
            "id": 148392,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>After including two parameters in the <code>.reduce()</code> inline function, what values do they give the inline function syntax access to?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The previous reduction value and the current array value</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The current array value and the previous reduction value</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The current array value and the calling array</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The previous reduction value and the current array value.</p></body></html>"
          }
        ]
